CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* alias in a member function template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* alias of the same name: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
N5008 [namespace.alias]/2: a namespace alias in a member function of a
class template made the type checker treat the alias's scope as a class
(an invariant failure, "... was not found"), and `namespace impl = impl;'
denoted the alias itself.
